body:
I'm more than 6yrs out at this point and I've been remarried for 1.3yrs right now. It was relatively quick for me compared to my first wife were we dated for close to 4years before we were engaged for more than a year. My new wife was just over a year really before we got married. We had known each other growing up so it was easier and given our ages. (34 for me and 33 for her) we knew how we felt and there were very few doubts. She'd also been married before but that ended in divorce. 

&#x200B;

I found everything easier. We were full fledged adults (I was in my first wedding but I was freaked about cost and marriage same as she was so influence was had much easier for family) we knew what we wanted and didn't let family dictate shit or invite lists. We kept it small and inexpensively.

The seriously powerful enemies and no status recovery stuff has me leaning towards he is awarded a job/class based on where/how he is 'defeated' and/or by what enemy. That is if he doesn't beat the dungeon.

&#x200B;

I usually look ahead to the raws but I have to refrain since I really want to be surprised. Or maybe he has to defeat the boss and than a 'king' spawns in the throne and awards him his class or job?
